 {"step_by_step_thinking": "The patient is a 17-year-old female admitted for living donor RTx. Her medical history includes malignant hypertension and ESRD. She was on maximum dosage of three types of antihypertensive drugs and regular hemodialysis. She developed seizures, headaches, altered consciousness, visual disturbances, and weakness. Her blood pressure was 210/110 mmHg, temperature was 38.3°C, and respiratory rate was 30 breaths per minute. Arterial blood gas showed pH 7.37, PaCO2 43 mmHg, and PaO2 137 mmHg. Fundoscopic examination revealed hypertensive retinopathy without papilledema, and non-contrast brain computed tomography showed bilateral symmetrical white matter hypodensity in the parietal, temporal, and occipital regions. She had no history of cytotoxic immunosuppressive therapy or eclampsia. Her laboratory investigations revealed a serum creatinine level of 7.2 mg/dl. 

The patient's race is not mentioned, so the default value of the race coefficient is 1.0. The patient is female, so the gender coefficient is 0.742. The patient's estimated GFR is calculated using the MDRD equation as: GFR = 175 * creatinine^(-1.154) * age^(-0.203) * race_coefficient * gender_coefficient. Plugging in these values will give us: 175 * 7.2^(-1.154) * 17^(-0.203) * 1 * 0.742 = 11.11 mL/min/1.73m².

Hence, the patient's GFR is 11.11 mL/min/1.73m².", "answer": 11.11}
